# Versioned search index: rebuild into a new physical index, verify, switch the alias, roll back.
# All routes need the admin key. They need an API started against your own MongoDB and OpenSearch with data in
# the supplier-a collection (see tools/Content.Seed). Run the requests top to bottom; the expected status code is written above each.

@host = http://localhost:5103
@readerKey = demo-reader-key-0000
@adminKey = demo-admin-key-0000
@alias = content-hotel_supplier-a

### Versions behind the alias before any rebuild: nothing current, nothing retained (200).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/index/{{alias}}
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Rebuild: fill a new index {alias}-vN, verify it, then switch the alias with one request (202).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/index/{{alias}}/rebuild
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "batchSize": 1000 }

### A second rebuild or a sync while it is active (409, problem+json).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/index/{{alias}}/rebuild
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Follow the rebuild: latestRun.state becomes "completed" (or "failed" with the verification result below) (200).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/index/{{alias}}
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Rebuild again so a previous version is retained for rollback (202).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/index/{{alias}}/rebuild
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Roll back to the most recently retired version (200). 409 while a run is active or when nothing is retained.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/index/{{alias}}/rollback
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Roll back to a named retained version (200, 409 if it is not retained, 400 if the number is not positive).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/index/{{alias}}/rollback
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 1 }

### An alias this service does not serve (404, problem+json).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/index/content-nowhere
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### A reader key on an admin route (403, problem+json).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/index/{{alias}}
X-Api-Key: {{readerKey}}
